<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>1.1.1: Understanding Value</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00051</md:content-id>
    <md:title>1.1.1: Understanding Value</md:title>
    <md:uuid>9cb229d9-e088-406f-86d8-23b14444af58</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section>
      <title>Warm Up Activity</title>
      <para>Here are some letters and what they represent. All costs are in dollars.</para>
      <list>
        <item>\( m \) represents the cost of a main dish.</item>
        <item>\( n \) represents the number of side dishes.</item>
        <item>\( s \) represents the cost of a side dish.</item>
        <item>\( t \) represents the total cost of a meal.</item>
      </list>
      <para>For questions 1 - 4, discuss what each <term class="glossary-tooltip">equation</term> means with a partner. Then, describe the situation in words.</para>
      <exercise>
        <problem>
          <para>\( m=7.50 \)</para>
        </problem>
        <solution>
          <para>Compare your answer:</para>
          <para>A main dish costs $7.50.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise>
        <problem>
          <para>\( m = s + 4.50 \)</para>
        </problem>
        <solution>
          <para>Compare your answer:</para>
          <para>Your answer may vary, but here are some examples.</para>
          <list>
            <item>The cost of a main dish is the cost of the side dish plus $4.50.</item>
            <item> The cost of a main dish is $4.50 more than the cost of a side dish.</item>
          </list>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise>
        <problem>
          <para>\( ns = 6 \)</para>
        </problem>
        <solution>
          <para>Compare your answer:</para>
          <para>The number of side dishes times the cost of the side dish is \($6\).</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise>
        <problem>
          <para>\( m + ns = t \)</para>
        </problem>
        <solution>
          <para>Compare your answer:</para>
          <para>The main dish added to the quantity of the number of side dishes times the cost of the side dish represents the total cost of the meal.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise>
        <problem>
          <para>Write a new equation that could be true in this same situation.</para>
        </problem>
        <solution>
          <para>Compare your answer:</para>
          <para>Your answer may vary, but here are some examples.</para>
          <list>
            <item>\(m = 2\)</item>
            <item> \(m - s = 4.5\)</item>
            <item> \(m + 6 = 13.5\)</item>
          </list>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise>
        <problem>
          <para>Describe what your new equation means in words.</para>
        </problem>
        <solution>
          <para>Compare your answer:</para>
          <para>Your answer may vary, but here are some examples.</para>
          <list>
            <item>The main dish costs \($2\).</item>
            <item> The difference in cost between the main dish and a side dish is \($4.50\).</item>
            <item> \($13.50\) is the cost of the main dish and a \($6\) tip.</item>
          </list>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
    </section>
  </content>
